Operator request: "How do we add this deep-research pattern to our regular loop
cycle to encourage ingestion of SOTA ideas in our bleeding-edge efforts?"

- CLAUDE.md: new "## SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline (MANDATORY)" — the planner
  reserves one ingestion slot per milestone that has a fork advancing an unsolved
  layer; the task reads research-studying.md + runs sweep_clusters/semscholar/
  citations helpers + low-concurrency WebSearch (NOT the /deep-research harness,
  which 429-failed 4x in the loop), and emits a dated SOTA->experiment mapping note.
- ops/known-issues.md: STANDING recurring priority "RESERVE A SOTA-INGESTION SLOT
  PER BLEEDING-EDGE MILESTONE" so the planner picks it up every milestone.
- research-roadmap-next.yaml: wired the .372 literature survey into the live forks
  — exp4021 (PHS*-guided search + hierarchical landmarks + per-step MPC replanning),
  exp4022 ("Invisible Leash" arXiv:2507.14843 as the distillation-vs-representation
  decider).

Exemplar of the output shape: docs/research-notes/search-layer-literature-2026-06-11.md

